A||N||40||2xsess||Some people just don't get it||||1||
Z||000000||2xsess||11-23-2000||11:41 AM||||This week I had to give three of my co-workers rides in my Fiero (no not at the same time <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) <P>The first one was like wow you have a trunk, but what good is it, look at how tiny it is. <P>The second one wanted to see what was under the hood and how big the trunk was so I opened it up and he just laughed, I was like "that's why I have a mini-van" But he thought the speaker seats were the coolest thing.<P>The third one ridiculed it the most. He complained about not being able to lay the seat back and having to get out because it's so low, (can't wait til I give him a ride after the springs go in) He called it a midget car. I told him , well you didn't have to ride in it, hop in your Fireturd that the heater doesn't work and drive yourself. That kind of shut him up. lol.<P>Well, just venting a little bit<P>HAPPY THANKSGIVING!!<P>Jeff<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||DavidHenshaw||11-23-2000||01:03 PM||||Jeff, the world is full of not very smart people. I want to share with you the TRUTH about the Fiero. When you get into the car you are experiencing something that few people are privileged to experience.<P>The car is low = great cornering<P>Hard to get into and out = only people who are smart enough keep reasonable control of thier weight can enjoy car. Others relagated to SUV's.<P>Trunk is small = can you believe pontiac engineers were able to include such a great trunk in such a fantastic car.<P>Car is beautiful = envy of other drivers which makes them critical as they try and level the playing field.<P>I could go on but you get the idea.<P><BR>Dave<P>86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||count von stewben||11-23-2000||01:32 PM||||So what are you saying fat people of very massive people are stupid and shouldnt have small cars?  Thats *&%$ up.  Tell me that if you are ever at a meet or something ok.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||2xsess||11-23-2000||01:36 PM||||David, I think you did go a little far with the weight control thing. The guy that was complaining about getting out of my car is thin but, he is about 6' tall. I'm also that tall it's just that I love the car and I'm used to it. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||count_iblis||11-23-2000||01:36 PM||||I am a very massive person.  So I guess I should be smart and get a suv and sell my Fiero.  I think some things should just not be said, and this is one of them.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/count-sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||onfire||11-23-2000||02:37 PM||||My brother is 6'6". He couldn't believe how much leg and head rooom there was. I think if he was any taller he would have started complaining. I don't think he would care for long rides either but he fit. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>"I seen it on the internet, and I believe everthing on the net."<BR><A HREF="http://homestead.deja.com/user.on_fire/on_fire.html" TARGET=_blank>Check out my waist of banbwidth.</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||StuGood||11-23-2000||02:40 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DavidHenshaw:<BR><B>Jeff, the world is full of not very smart people... --- beautiful = envy of other drivers which makes them critical as they try and level the playing field...<BR>86 GT</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Face it, like Benson & Hedges used to say, Fieros aren't for everybody.  So you don't have to try to "sell" everybody on them.  Just be glad <B>you</B> have a car that you care about and enjoy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">!<P>I understand your enthusiasm, but I very seldom "have" to offer other people rides in my Fieros.  I wait until <B>they</B> ask, or until a situation comes up where they need a ride (e.g. - when their relatively new car quits  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">).  It comes up often enough.  And when it does, they are often suddenly rather impressed with how nice Fieros are- lots of questions and favorable comments.<P>My favorite response to criticism of Fieros is to smile and say, "fine  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">."  Try it sometime- even if the comments are plainly wrong.  The implication, of course, is that they don't know what they're talking about (which is frequently the case).  If you keep your cool, it will absolutely infuriate them  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">.  And just keep enjoying your Fiero, even if you're the only one who knows what great cars they really are  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> !||||reg||14
Z||000007||Philphine||11-23-2000||02:49 PM||||i think the car either didn't stay on the market long enough or got the fire rep smeared on it too hard for people to really know what the car is about. i've talked off and on with the people i work with who didn't realise things like the 4 wheel independent suspension or 4 wheel disc brakes, or the improvements that can be made performance wise (engine,etc.). i recently mentioned that i was considering selling the cheap fiero i got from the dav lot and one person was immediatly interested. got 'em thinkin'<P>also occassionally some one will ask about my '87 and say they've seen it around town. if i ever get a swap made i think it will make people give fieros a rethink around here even without trying to race anyone i see. a lot of people don't know about the body mods available few that they are, and i always try to mention how mustang wings fit on them (coupes anyway) 'cause thats some thing that can be easy to get and /or try. <P>keep foolin' with 'em.  <P>------------------<BR>Phil T<P>'87 coupe (feral)<BR>'84 indy<BR>'84 coupe (cheap thrill)||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fformula88||11-23-2000||03:03 PM||||I find the best way to cure people'sm bad ideas about the Fiero is to take them for a ride in one.  No matter what their gripe may be, I can usually let them leave grinning after a quick spin!  <P>I had a co-worker who owned a Mazda MPV.  He was always making fun of my car until one day we came out to go home and his "SUV" had a flat tire.  I stuck around to help him change it and we found the spare was flat as well.  I offered to drive him and a spare to the garage for air.  He didn't think it was possible, but the Fiero trunk easily swallowed his tire and rim and we were off.  Ever since he has loved my car! <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">  <BR>1988 Fiero Formula||||reg||1
Z||000009||DaRkLoRD||11-23-2000||04:04 PM||||The biggest complaint I have about getting in and out of the Fiero, are those stupid vent things that stick way out by the doors... I've smacked my knee on them many times....<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||8
Z||000010||zeusrekning||11-23-2000||04:11 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DavidHenshaw:<BR><B>Hard to get into and out = only people who are smart enough keep reasonable control of thier weight can enjoy car. Others relagated to SUV's.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I was guessing he meant control as in controling balance. I was thinking the same thing when i got in my fiero an hour ago to go eat ThanksGiving dinner. I'm 5'11 and about 165 lbs but you can't just fall into the car.<BR>What got me thinking this is the rip in the seat about halfway up. <BR>Seat ripped there and so did fairly new seat cover guessing i wasn't controling my balance when getting in and out. i rub that rip everytime.<BR>My dad is a little bit larger and a good bit older and it was funny watching him get in and out.<BR>But i belive you have to control your balance to get in and out easier.<P><BR>Now C.S. When my dad owned my fiero he gave a guy who worked with him a ride and the guy kept complaing and putting down the fiero.<BR>"too small", "too hard to get in " etc<BR>But all the guy had was a bike and it was raining. No gratitude. Gets a ride so he didn't have to peddal in the rain and he talks junk about the car. ||||reg||1
Z||000011||sqoach||11-23-2000||09:55 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DaRkLoRD:<BR><B>The biggest complaint I have about getting in and out of the Fiero, are those stupid vent things that stick way out by the doors... I've smacked my knee on them many times....<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>i've had a few complaints about that too.  you can easily tell my passengers have hit that vent because it is cracked.  the drivers side is too, but not because of me.  of course i'm only 5'9 and 160 lbs so it's kinda easy for me to get in and out.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>sQoaCh||||reg||1
Z||000012||Phil||11-23-2000||10:06 PM||||I'm 6 ft. tall and about 205 lbs. and I've driven my beast 40000 mi in the last 15 months with no fitment probs.<P>------------------<BR> <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/New-sig.jpg"> <BR>SC 3800||||reg||1
Z||000013||RaeQwan||11-23-2000||10:09 PM||||I myself am only about 6'2-6'3, I've never had any problems getting in or out of my 88 or my brothers 87, I have however had a hell of a time getting in and out of SUV's my family has had. My brother is 6'8, I've never heard him complain out about getting in or out of his 87. the only person who has really complained about getting in nd out of my car are short ppl. and well, LARGE people.<P>*puts on a flame suit*<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/raeqwancfa.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||JBGehling||11-23-2000||10:44 PM||||Ever since I got my first Fiero about five months ago, I've heard nothing but trash from everyone at school  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. The first day I got it, I was trying to talk about the car with one of my friends and he calls it "a sports car wannabe" (he drives a 70's VW van). One that really hurt was when my old girlfriend asked me "Do you really like that car" (although she had only seen a really trashy 87 GT in the parking lot and not my 88 GT &lt;trashy meaning it was in bad condition, not that 88's look better than 87's  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">). And she then commenced to tell me about her boyfriends car (80's Z-28 Camaro) of which she bragged was the fastest car in South Carolina! lol. <BR>Just when I thought the humiliation was over  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">, a few weeks ago, I was reading the Fiero road test book at school when one of the kid's called in "a mexican sports car" (turns to his friends) "I mean look at it, it's mexican, even "fiero" is a mexican word" (I thought this was pretty funny but it still made me pretty mad  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)... "it's italian" I said, and it seemed to quiet them down a little! <BR>But this stuff only gets to me some of the time, when I'm on the road, nothing compares to fun I have in a Fiero!<P>Josh<P>You don't even wanna know what people say when I've told them that I'm interested in a delorean ("that's the ugliest car I've ever seen"!)||||reg||1
Z||000015||JBGehling||11-23-2000||10:47 PM||||Sorry about the mistakes above, I didn't bother to proofread.<BR>Josh||||reg||1
Z||000016||Black88GT||11-23-2000||11:07 PM||||Darklord, thats why so many people have those cracks where the vents are!  My sister did that once but she didn't crack it, I could have killed her!<P>I find the best way to get in is head first, then swing your body in.  This prevents the two biggest wear marks on any Fiero, the drivers seat pad and the dash vents.  Looks kinda funny though but it works.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||DaRkLoRD||11-24-2000||12:02 AM||||What's the point in having the vents stick out so far?? in most of the aftermarket dashes I've seen, they're not sticking out, so I assume there's no real reason...<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||5
Z||000018||fldevel||11-24-2000||12:15 AM|||| my brother in law used to think his BMW was the coolist thing till i took him for a ride one day to the 7-11 while going around a corner at about 35mph  "90 dagree turn" without the tires even breaking loose, it kinda put a smile on my face when he replied "this B***H is awesome" ..||||reg||11
Z||000019||DaRkLoRD||11-24-2000||12:29 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>Darklord, thats why so many people have those cracks where the vents are!  My sister did that once but she didn't crack it, I could have killed her!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hmm.. if my sister did that (I doubt she would though, she's about 5'5", and very light..) I'd be slightly ticked off.. but I wouldn't get really mad for 2 reasons.. I think the fiero interior is one of the ugliest I've ever seen, and plan to scrap it for an aftermarket one as soon as I can afford to.. and second, my sister is WAY more important to me than a car........<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000020||2xsess||11-24-2000||11:02 PM||||You should see people's faces when I tell them I'm going to lower it too. My wife said how much lower can it go?lol<P>My wife hates Fieros she doesn't even ride in mine, whenever we go somewhere we take the Transport. <P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000021||MikeE||11-25-2000||06:10 AM||||Hey, let's face it, the trunk is small, but at least it's hot, LOL.<P>Next time tell them, it may be small, but I can pop popcorn in it.||||reg||1
Z||000022||NoWing87||11-26-2000||08:01 AM||||Bottom line folks...People that talk trash about Fieros have never owned one, never driven one and are completely ignorant of all the favorable qualities.<P>None of my family or friends understand my fascination; and that's o.k. with me. I don't even try to make them understand any more. I just pass them and out-corner them all while getting better gas mileage!!!||||reg||1
Z||000023||DJRice||11-27-2000||09:53 AM||||FYI, The Fiero trunk is just big enough to carry two "airplane carry-on size" suitcases side by side.  <P>I guess riding in a Fiero is kinda like flying.   ||||reg||1
Z||000024||84 Indy||11-29-2000||10:15 PM||||I used to hate these cars till my brother gave me my first one. I needed a car but i wanted anything but a Fiero at that time i would have rathered a Renualt LeCar. I finally took the piece of crap that i now love and have loved since the first day i drove it. I still drive my first Fiero almost everyday. And now have four i think it's the best cars i ever had. I feel if they don't like them than WALK!!!!||||reg||10
Z||000025||GarethWright||11-30-2000||12:33 AM||||Everyone keeps telling me my '87 GT is too small, but for me its a step Up in size, thats right, my last car was a '76 MG Midget, you wanna see something funny, watch a 6'4 (not me) guy try to get outta one of those!  At least on the Fiero the door hinges up front, on the Midget the door opening reached from just behind the seat, to about even with the knees when sitting in it!  <BR>Both Low, both tons of fun, unfortunatly the MG was rear-ended by a Jeep Grand Cherokee  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  But i got enough cash from insurance to get the Fiero  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000026||2xsess||11-30-2000||07:51 AM||||I just laugh it off. I like my small cars, anyone ever tried to sit in the backseat of a firebird or an eclipse? might as well not even be one. I know it helps keep their insurance rates down.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000027||Raydar||11-30-2000||01:33 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 2xsess:<BR><B>You should see people's faces when I tell them I'm going to lower it too. My wife said how much lower can it go?lol<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I never really noticed how low the Fiero was until I was driving in downtown Atlanta behind an MGB, and was looking <I>up</I> at it.<P>Raydar<P>||||reg||1
Z||000028||Steven||11-30-2000||02:00 PM||||If you think dealing with all of the people out there that hate/dislike/misunderstand Fieros is bad, be happy. You can take them for a ride in yours and show them how great it is. Mine has been down since May, and all I keep hearing is how bad my car is. When I try to argue with them that it is a good car, they remind me that no car of theirs ever took 7 months and counting to repair. Their is no defense for that statement. You just have to put tail between legs and walk off mumbling something about how one day it will be done, and you will show them...you will show them all! Has anyone seen my medicine? I will feel better after I take it. <p>[This message has been edited by Steven (edited 11-30-2000).]||||reg||8
Z||000029||PearlBlueSoul||11-30-2000||03:04 PM||||Eh, I get insults too.  Dont' think for a moment that we don't get slided.<P>I get the usual, "rice burner" insults, and how it's so small, and how I can't fit a system in it, how it's not as fast as this car or that car, how it can't beat this and that.  I'm just kinda like, "well, I know it can, and you've never ridden in my car.  so how do you know?"  Every time I bring it to a car show though at my school, it gets a crowd around it all day long.  It really depends on who you're talking to.  If you're talking to guys that are used to Front engine, front drive, it may seem strange that america copied a european design.  <P>I haven't had complaints about my car being too low (yet) but I know what you all mean.  my car is at my ankle when I get out now (since I've lowered it).  When i rode in 1FSTM6's fiero, I noticed I fell into it like I did when my dad had his 93 vette.  I kinda liked it tho, being so low to the ground makes me feel more secure soemhow.  And yes!  I get that dwarf syndrome on barett parkway.  my worst fears are getting packed in on all 4 cardinal directions by SUVs, or even semis!  That's when I find 3rd gear, and about 6800 RPM  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.<P>------------------<BR>1987 Toyota MR2 N/A 5 speed<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.atlantamr2s.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.atlantamr2s.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/darionscard</A>  <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard/Thumb.jpg">       <BR><B>Notable mods:</B>  Sus tech springs and sway bars, Toyota strut tower brace, KYB strut inserts, HKS exhaust, NGK plugs/wires, Momo Racer wheels (14x6), Custom intake, Kenwood 12" speaker in front trunk, Jensen amp.||||reg||1
Z||000030||william_thorniii||11-30-2000||03:31 PM||||Steven,<P>Sorry to hear about your troubles.  You have stumbled on to the right place to get your car back on the road again.<P>I went to university in Flint and worked for a Professor in White Lake (exit 77?) off of I-75.  Is this the same White Lake, MI?  If so there are tons of local "fieroholics" around that should easily be able to help you out.  OTW post a good, detailed description of your problems in the Technical section and I am sure that your problem will be improved.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||13
Z||000031||Tigger||11-30-2000||03:38 PM||||Just last week the rear drum brake in my '85 Regal came apart, creating a nasty shake/vibration upon braking.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>The next day, I got talking with my boss at work about what had happened with my Regal.  Near the end of the conversation he says, "Boy, that Fiero has been a lot of problems hasn't it, what next will go on it?"  I kindly told him "No, it was my Regal," and also informed him that Fiero's have all wheel disc brakes, no drums.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>I had to laugh afterwards because during the whole conversation he was trying to be-little my car, and I couldn't figure why, didn't occur to me at the time he was making assumptions that the problems were with my Fiero.<P>Gee Wiz, give the Fiero a break! (no pun intended)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue2.gif"> ||||reg||8
Z||000032||Steven||11-30-2000||03:49 PM||||I am not having a problem that I can't figure out, unless finding time to work on it counts. It had a timing chain replaced about 2 years ago. Something happened to the timing chain. I don't know if it was just a bad heat treat on bad gear, but the chain tried to walk closer to the timing cover. Well that was when the "build a 3.2 liter, it is easy" idea came to mind. Machine work is done on block, parts are all ordered and received, just need to finish heads, asmemble engine, and install. ||||reg||1
Z||000033||Raydar||11-30-2000||05:16 PM||||When you figure out that "finding time to work on it" thing, Please let me know. I have the same problem.<BR>Good luck with your build.<P>Raydar||||reg||1
Z||000034||william_thorniii||11-30-2000||05:29 PM||||Raydar,<P>The best suggestion I can give you for "finding time" would to be to cancel your cable & home internet service.  Since I moved a few months ago, I haven't had everything re-installed.  This has proven to be the most productive thing I have ever done.  <P>I do miss the Simpsons and HBO though.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||14
Z||000035||sqoach||11-30-2000||05:48 PM||||hmm...i guess i can comment on this topic.  when i first got my fiero, a lot of people made fun of it because it's so small.  they'd call it a toy, so i decided to get my hotwheels plate on the front  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> i think of my car as a toy i guess.  it's fun.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>i didn't realize how small it was, though, until i let my friend drive it and i was in his civic.  i looked down and started laughing.  but it's all good.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P>------------------<BR>sQoaCh||||reg||1
Z||000036||Zorba||11-30-2000||05:58 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 2xsess:<BR><B> The first one was like wow you have a trunk, but what good is it, look at how tiny it is. <P> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Average people drive average cars and usually produce predictable average comments. This makes all the car manufacturers very happy. Ever wonder why there is so little individuality in cars. They are all mass produced and about the same. When they are not, they call them "exotics"...So you can expect dumb comments about the fiero, ferrari, boxters,<BR>miatas, etc...that's because they are not cars for the masses. To each his own.<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000037||2xsess||11-30-2000||06:14 PM||||Very Well put Zorba  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I really don't een pay them any mind anymore. When someone says something about being scared to ride in one I just whip out the pictures I have of my 88 without the bodypanels. They soon change their tune.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>I used to let it get to me though. I think the worst thing I ever heard was, one time I took my car into a technical school I was attending and a woman standing there said "oh look it's a tupperware car" I felt much better when I saw her walk out and get into an old rusted out Nova. <P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000038||rogergarrison||12-01-2000||05:55 PM||||im 6' and i dont have any more trouble getting in and out than any other car. hardest to me is a corvette with those huge door sills. im very comfortable driving in mine for 5 or 6 hours on end without any aches or pains. Ive had people for rides that are very impressed with performance. I have a modified 3.1 with turbo and the 410 4-speed. Im gonna have to actually measure my 0-60 and 0-100 times for the hell of it. I rarely get beat on a freeway race. all i know is low gear winds up to 7,000 rpm in a few seconds, around prob 30mph. I just like smiling stupidly as i pass them in my little tiny toy car, lol||||reg||1
Z||000039||jerpro||12-02-2000||12:54 PM||||I am 6,2 and 210 pounds. I love my fiero and would change it for nothing.<BR>I have recievd several insults, mainly nonsense.<BR>All I do is look at their old rusty car, stare and give a BIIIIIG smile  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <BR>that shuts them up HA!<P>------------------<BR>Only try your best, and if you don't succeed... TRY HARDER.||||reg||1
Z||000040||Phil||12-02-2000||01:19 PM||||Here is enough stuff for a 3 week road trip for 2 people<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/trunk_2.jpg">  <BR>Had to resize pic<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Phil (edited 12-02-2000).]||||reg||1
